There are many vegetables on the cart.
I see a strange vegetable.
It is dark green in colour.
It is a little bumpy on the outside.
I do not eat this vegetable in Mexico.
I do not know its name.
I show that vegetable to the vendor.
I ask, "Bhaiya, what is this?"
The vendor smiles.
He says, "Madam, this is karela."
I ask, "Is this vegetable good?"
He explains, "It is very good for health."
"But it is a little bitter."
I think for a while.
I do not like bitter food at all.
I tell the vendor.
"Bhaiya, I do not want karela today."
"I only want tomatoes and spinach."
The vendor says, "No problem, Madam."
